      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-50500",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the sequence $a_{n} = \\frac{1}{n}$. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $a_{n}$ is positive and decreasing for all $n \\ge 1$.\n2. $lim_(n \u2192 \u221e)a_{n} = 0$.\n3. By the alternating test, the series $\u2211_(n = 1)^(\u221e)((-1)^{n})/(n)$ is convergent."
